## Reading Settings with IConfiguration

Almost every real .NET application needs externally adjustable settings -- connection strings, feature flags, API keys -- without hard-coding them into source. .NET's configuration system solves this with `appsettings.json` and the `IConfiguration` abstraction.

By default, an ASP.NET Core (or generic host) application automatically loads `appsettings.json` from the project's root and exposes its contents through `IConfiguration`, which you can inject anywhere via dependency injection. Nested JSON objects become colon-separated keys, so a value at `Mail.MaxRetries` in the JSON is read as `"Mail:MaxRetries"`.

```json
{
  "ConnectionStrings": {
    "Default": "Server=localhost;Database=Shop;Trusted_Connection=True;"
  },
  "Mail": {
    "FromAddress": "no-reply@example.com",
    "MaxRetries": 3
  }
}
```

`IConfiguration` exposes values two main ways: indexer access (`config["Mail:MaxRetries"]`), which always returns a `string?`, and `GetValue<T>("key")`, which parses the string into the requested type. `GetSection("Mail")` returns an `IConfigurationSection` scoped to that nested object, letting you work with a sub-tree without repeating the prefix everywhere.

```csharp
var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);
var app = builder.Build();

app.MapGet("/config-demo", (IConfiguration config) =>
{
    int maxRetries = config.GetValue<int>("Mail:MaxRetries");
    return $"Retries allowed: {maxRetries}";
});

app.Run();
```

- Colons (`:`) separate nested JSON keys when read as a flat key string.
- `GetValue<T>` performs type conversion; the indexer always returns `string?`.
- `GetSection` scopes access to a sub-tree, and also supports binding straight to an object with `Bind(...)`.
- Configuration is read-only from the application's perspective at run time (changing the underlying file can trigger a reload if `reloadOnChange: true`, but your code never writes configuration back).

codeExamples.code:
var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);
var app = builder.Build();

app.MapGet("/config-demo", (IConfiguration config) =>
{
    int maxRetries = config.GetValue<int>("Mail:MaxRetries");
    return $"Retries allowed: {maxRetries}";
});

app.Run();

